---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const entries = [
  {
    day: 'WEEK 1: 09/14/2026',
    title: 'Picking a direction.',
    text: [
      `I started out feeling stuck because the assignment was simply to build a website. I had a lot of freedom, but I did not know where to start or which choice to make first.`,
      `Having AI make a first pass gave me something concrete to react to. That helped me choose a project about using AI to help with Pointwise Glyph meshing, mesh checks, and grid-convergence studies. I am still figuring out how much I should decide on my own before I ask a model to help me explore ideas.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    day: 'WEEK 1: 09/15/2026',
    title: 'Building the site.',
    text: [
      `I looked at classmate Hugh Cairney’s Astro and Tailwind setup, then built a simple four-page site with a shared layout. Once I knew I liked compact labels, thin rules, square panels, and graph-paper-inspired log cards, the site came together much more quickly.`,
      `At first, website generation was frustrating. Even the highest-level models from each company would run ahead and add pages, features, or styling that I had not asked for. Now I ask for a plan first and say that I need to approve it before any design or code changes. That helps keep the site simple and closer to what I actually want.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    day: 'WEEK 1: 09/15/2026',
    title: 'Trying models for animation.',
    text: [
      `While building the small interactive parts of the site, I tried GPT-5.6 Terra and Claude Sonnet 4.6 for canvas animations. The Claude version looked cleaner and took less work to fit into the site.`,
      `That made me think more about which jobs each model is good at. I do not want to assume that the most advanced version of a model will be best for every task. I want to keep comparing them, especially for visual work where something can look good at first but still need a lot of fixing.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    day: 'WEEK 2: 09/22/2026',
    title: 'Making a notation-consistency skill.',
    text: [
      `This week I considered making a skill for engineering reasoning, technical writing, or plotting. I chose technical writing because I wanted to learn how skills are put together before trying something more complicated. I made an equation and notation consistency checker for a problem I have in longer fluid- and solid-mechanics documents: using different subscripts, symbols, or conventions for the same quantity. I started with a real thesis example about vibrational-temperature subscripts, then used other examples to improve the instructions and cut down on false alarms.`,
      `The biggest lesson was that it is much easier to make a skill when the job is narrow and clear. I also spent time trying to fix Pi directory and write-permission problems that continued after restarting and updating it. I have not fixed that yet, but it has made me pay more attention to the setup around an agent, not just the prompts I give it.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    day: 'WEEK 2: 09/24/2026',
    title: 'Trying class skills and refining the project.',
    text: [
      `I looked through the class skills and liked that grill-me and fight-me work at different levels. I can see them being useful at different points in the research process. I copied both into my skills folder and tried adding a short section at the bottom to prime them to be even harsher about CFD and numerical-method claims. I want them to push me to be precise about what I mean and how I will support it. They gave me a few comments that were a little harsh, but needed, about my scope being broad. I will keep that in mind as I move forward and see how the exact metric for reduced meshing time takes shape.`, 
      `After meeting with my advisor, Professor Harris, last Monday, I finalized the agent-assisted meshing procedure in my one-pager. I also refined the website so it reflects that same procedure and better shows what I am planning to do.`,
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Dev log" description="Development notes for Madison Taylor Hobbs's AI research portfolio.">
  <section class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.14em] text-red-accent">DEVELOPMENT LOG</p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 font-display text-5xl font-medium tracking-[-0.06em] sm:text-6xl">Notes from the work.</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-graphite">A concise record of how this project and portfolio are taking shape, including what I asked AI tools to help with and what I reviewed myself.</p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5">
      {entries.map((entry) => (
        <article class="paper-grid border border-rule p-5 sm:p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.12em] text-red-accent">{entry.day}</p>
          <h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.04em]">{entry.title}</h2>
          <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 leading-7 text-graphite">
            {entry.text.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
